    4	Thread 5 (commit). The S202 unified theorem closed Thread 3 (Galway frontier)
    5	*per query* under Montgomery: K*(x, p) = Theta-tilde(x) zeros are required
    6	for pi(x) +/- 1 in distribution at any positive hit-rate. But Riemann zeros
    7	are properties of zeta, not x. If K zeros are computed once and reused across
    8	M batched queries pi(x_1), ..., pi(x_M), per-x cost decomposes:
    9	
    10	    T_total(K, M, x_max, x_1..M) = T_setup(K) + sum_{i=1}^M T_eval(K, x_i),
    11	
    12	so amortised per-x cost is
    13	
    14	    T_per_x_amortised = T_setup(K) / M + T_eval_avg(K).
    15	
    16	Slot 1's job: measure T_setup(K) and T_eval(K, x) separately, characterise
