    18	profile under any choice of M and x-distribution.
    19	
    20	The empirical question this slot answers concretely:
    21	  (Q1) Is T_eval(K, x) approximately linear in K?
    22	  (Q2) Is T_eval(K, x)/K approximately x-independent?
    23	  (Q3) How does T_setup(K) scale with K (cache load vs from-scratch)?
    24	
    25	If Q1+Q2 hold, then per-x evaluation is asymptotically Theta(K) regardless
    26	of x, and the only knob to lower per-x amortised cost is K itself; any
    27	useful cross-x amortisation must come from setup amortisation, which is
    28	amortisable across M (T_setup/M -> 0) but cannot reduce the T_eval term.
