    13	S82-thesis criterion directly: "the eigenvector is character-aligned."
    14	
    15	Direct rule: k_char(d) = max k such that the k-th right-singular-vector
    16	has dominant centered residue energy (over Z/qZ for some q) > τ.
    17	
    18	If S82's character-vector identification is intrinsic to the spike block,
    19	then k_char ≈ k_canonical and the fractions should agree. If they
    20	disagree substantially, then S169 is counting additional sigmas that are
    21	NOT cleanly character-aligned, and the "spike block = character-vector
    22	energy" thesis weakens at the canonical boundary.
